  "worked_solution": "First, we note that $\\sqrt{121}=11$ is a natural number, so it belongs to $N.$\n\nSince every natural number is also an integer number, $\\sqrt{121}$ also belongs to $Z.$ \n\nOn the other hand, the sets ${Z}^{-}$ and ${Q}^{-}$ only contain negative numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{121}$ does not belong to either of these sets. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"",
